; Example: UEB emergency-stop reaction (copy to 0:/sys/trigger2.g).
; Fired by M581 in estop.g when the E-stop is pressed.
;
; Order matters: drop relay FIRST so that releasing the E-stop cannot
; re-energise the drives without a fresh safety check, set the light red
; (the daemon stops running after M112, so we set it here directly), then
; emergency-stop. No M400 - an E-stop must not wait for queued moves.
; Literal P5 (Scylla PD_5) — do not depend on nxtRelayID here.

M42 P5 S0                              ; gpOut OFF - contactor stays open until re-armed
M150 E0 R255 U0 B0 P255 S32 F0         ; strip RED - emergency stopped
M112                                   ; emergency stop - reset (M999) to recover
